WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.224 --> 00:00:03.131
♪ [music] ♪

00:00:05.700 --> 00:00:07.820
Give me one minute, and I'll show you

00:00:07.820 --> 00:00:09.941
how Google Cloud Public Datasets

00:00:09.941 --> 00:00:13.041
can add value to your analytics
and AI initiatives.

00:00:13.573 --> 00:00:15.356
With over 200 datasets

00:00:15.356 --> 00:00:18.083
representing more than
20 petabytes of data,

00:00:18.083 --> 00:00:21.890
the Public Datasets program hosts 
all types of in-demand data,

00:00:21.890 --> 00:00:24.872
from convenient geographic and census data

00:00:24.872 --> 00:00:27.937
to high impact datasets for COVID-19,

00:00:27.937 --> 00:00:31.217
to weather and climate data 
from providers like NOAA.

00:00:31.217 --> 00:00:33.328
The best part is that the procurement,

00:00:33.328 --> 00:00:35.943
pipeline building
and maintenance, and hosting,

00:00:35.943 --> 00:00:37.435
is all taken care of,

00:00:37.435 --> 00:00:39.329
so you can dive straight into enriching

00:00:39.329 --> 00:00:41.223
your analyses or AI projects.

00:00:42.384 --> 00:00:43.436
To get started,

00:00:43.436 --> 00:00:46.351
head to the Marketplace
in the Google Cloud console,

00:00:46.351 --> 00:00:48.376
where you can explore all the datasets,

00:00:48.376 --> 00:00:51.266
their metadata, and see example queries.

00:00:52.504 --> 00:00:54.979
Once you found a dataset 
you're interested in,

00:00:54.979 --> 00:00:56.187
click to view the dataset

00:00:56.187 --> 00:00:59.532
where you can start analyzing it
alongside your own data.

00:01:00.215 --> 00:01:03.463
If you're new to BigQuery,
check out the BigQuery sandbox,

00:01:03.463 --> 00:01:06.628
which includes 1 terabyte
of querying free each month

00:01:06.628 --> 00:01:08.379
without needing a credit card.

00:01:09.345 --> 00:01:11.356
So next time you're looking to strengthen

00:01:11.356 --> 00:01:13.697
your analytics and drive new insights,

00:01:13.697 --> 00:01:16.310
take a look at Google Cloud
Public Datasets.

00:01:18.728 --> 00:01:23.175
To learn more, check out
<i>cloud.google.com/public-datasets</i>

